  "conclusion": "In the frozen batch, two of four lifetime-instrumented runs passed a parameter address to the native-call sequence after its storage had been freed on another thread. All eight controls completed without angular guards; one instrumented run failed the separate wire audit. One prior exploratory run also captured a freed handoff. The original Command constructor only stores raw pointers. This demonstrates unsafe lifetime ordering in this instrumented bridge, but does not observe a downstream freed-memory read or identify the cause of historical physical impulses."
